        ],
        "content": "Here’s a set of short, instantly readable, slightly silly-but-not-babyish councilor names that scream exactly what they do in CK2. No long fantasy names, no historical pretension, just pure function with a smirk.\n\n**Council positions (the six classic ones)**  \n- Lord Chancellor (Diplomacy) → **Charm**  \n- Marshal (Martial) → **Stab**  \n- Steward (Stewardship) → **Coin**  \n- Spymaster (Intrigue) → **Sneak**  \n- Court Chaplain (Learning) → **Pray** (covers the religious stuff)  \n- Court Physician (also Learning) → **Patch** (so you can tell Pray and Patch apart at a glance)\n\n**Your three permanent commanders**  \n- Left flank (movement speed guy) → **Zoom**  \n- Center (pagan/heretic damage guy) → **Smite**  \n- Right flank (siege speed guy) → **Batter**\n\n**Wife**  \nKeep her as **Wifey** (it’s already perfect) or upgrade to **Queenbee** if you want something equally clear but a bit spicier.\n\nFull council screen now looks like:  \nCharm · Stab · Coin · Sneak · Pray · Patch  \nCommanders: Zoom · Smite · Batter  \nConsort: Wifey (or Queenbee)\n\nZero imagination required, zero confusion possible, maximum medieval meme energy achieved. Enjoy your perfectly labeled murder-spreadsheet.",
