          "019d4f17-7de6-7f04-8fd2-b3eb2910e8b9"
        ],
        "content": "Here’s a more serious (but still short and crystal-clear) version with proper surnames. I gave them all the same dynasty name “de Functio” (Latin for “of the function”) so they feel like a coherent team of ultra-specialized professionals your court hired explicitly for the job.\n\n| Role                  | Name                         | What you instantly read                                          |\n|-----------------------|------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Chancellor (Diplomacy)| Lord Etienne de Functio      | “Etiquette” → diplomat                                          |\n| Marshal (Martial)     | Sir Balian de Functio        | “Valiant” with a B → martial beast                               |\n| Steward (Stewardship) | Master Renaud de Functio     | “Revenue” → money guy                                            |\n| Spymaster (Intrigue)  | Lady Morgaine de Functio     | “Morgana” → obvious intrigue vibes                               |\n| Court Chaplain        | Bishop Aldric de Functio     | “Aldric” sounds very churchy                                     |\n| Court Physician       | Master Gerard de Functio     | Classic physician name, keeps him distinct from the bishop      |\n| Commander – Left      | Captain Swift de Functio     | Literally the fast-march guy                                     |\n| Commander – Center    | Captain Crusader de Functio  | The holy-war damage monster                                      |\n| Commander – Right     | Captain Ram de Functio       | Siege engines go brrrrr                                          |\n| Wife                  | Lady [Your Dynasty] (Wifey)  | Keep the nickname privately, publicly she’s just your proper consort |\n\nIf you want them to feel even more like a single “department” you can shorten the dynasty to just **de Func** (still reads as noble):\n\n- Etienne de Func  \n- Balian de Func  \n- Renaud de Func  \netc.\n\nShort, dead serious on the council screen, and you’ll never forget who does what.",
